hey everyone how's it going and happy  new year  my name is mayuko and welcome back to my  channel where we talk about tech  career and life so it is finally 2021  and what better way to start off the  year on my channel than with an  intentions video in previous years i've  done like a last year reflections and  this year aspirations video  but 2020 was like a year  obviously events and themes from last  year are gonna come up because we're  always building upon the previous year  but i just kind of wanted to talk about  intentions today  and specifically i want to talk about  intentions not goals because  goals just makes me like feel a little  bit more stressed out like i either  achieved them or i didn't versus  intentions is like i'm orienting myself  towards a certain direction  i don't really know where i'm gonna end  up but these are kind of themes that i'm  going to  play into my year and we'll see how  things turn out  and quickly before we get started i  wanted to say thank you to the sponsor  of today's video  book of the month i know that a lot of  us have aspirations for  books that we want to read this year and  so i think book of the month is a great  service to do so  book of the month is a super popular  fast growing online book service for  readers  i've actually been subscribed to book of  the month previously and so i'm really  excited to be working with them their  whole mission is to promote  new and emerging authors and help  readers discover what books they love  their team vets hundreds of books each  month and gives readers their choice  from a curated selection of new  and early release titles so you can  spend more time reading and less time  researching  book of the month is also risk free so  you can skip any month  anytime and you will not be charged and  one of the biggest perks is that they  have the best price for new hardcover  fiction for january out of the five  books that they have  i chose the dating plan by sarah desai i  chose this one and i'm really excited to  read it because it's a love story about  a software engineer and i was like  it's me this one's for me so you can get  your very first book for just 9.99 by  using the code new books or by clicking  the link in the description box down  below  thank you again and book of the month  for sponsoring today's video and now  let's get back into it  so my intentions for 2021 is generally  to  number one level up and number two to  get to know myself better and ground  myself  this is like day six of 2021 by the way  and it's still kind of formulating in my  brain but that's kind of where i'm  headed towards at least  so as far as leveling up goes 2020 was  an interesting year for me  in that i feel like i've learned so many  new skills  and some of that was necessitated by  covid like  learning how to cut hair or learning how  to make bread  or getting better at cooking other  skills were related to my big career  change so  everything to do with the video stuff  and managing a business  and doing full-time youtube that was  also a ton of skills learned in the last  year  last year was a big year for me in my  anxiety after i had a really bad panic  attack at the end of 2019  and so i've been able to work on these  coping skills that i learned from my  therapist and have built a really good  foundation for how to cope with my  anxiety  and then some things i just like went  for it because they just became my new  hobby so i learned how to do woodworking  last year which was totally unexpected  and had no purpose at all other than i  just wanted to make something with my  hands  and that includes like building and  sanding and refinishing and also  sometimes upholstering things  but really i'm just surprised by like  how many things i was able to learn last  year and i think that's because in  previous years i used to think i  should be doing something or i should be  learning something  but last year i kind of just like let go  of that you know because 2020 was  absolutely wild and i was dealing with  my anxiety where i was afraid of  everything  and so a lot of the things that i did  was out of me wanting to do things or  realizing that i could do these things  like for the first time i feel like i  was just like bold or maybe just didn't  care  that much to overthink all the things  that i wanted to do  and i just did them i don't know if i'm  making sense but i feel like in previous  years i used to just like obsess over  like maybe i could be doing this  or i should be doing that or like oh my  god i should be somewhere by now but  it's  i just never did it because i think i  was too scared to i don't know maybe  it's like a late 20s thing where i just  started to gain more confidence  and just feel like more at peace with  myself and it wasn't confidence in like  a  oh my gosh i'm like the best at  everything and instead it was like a  you know i don't know anything i don't  know how to do this at all but  with time i could probably figure it out  i think a big part of it that was  probably my therapist  yeah doing weekly therapy was incredibly  helpful in 2020. so yeah in 2020 like  obviously there was a lot of change  happening i moved i changed jobs  but really i feel like kind of a  different person like i feel like the  biggest  change was within so last year really  was just kind of like  lots of new beginnings and building a  really strong foundation  so this year is all about leveling all  those things up  i think like i really want to get better  at woodworking i want to read a book  every month i want to work out more  consistently  i want to make the perfect cup of coffee  and i think related to  having this strong foundation of feeling  at peace with myself  is this whole getting to know myself  better and  grounding myself even further i was  watching my 2020 aspirations video and a  lot of it was  around just like grounding myself and  feeling calm and  peace making sure that i practice  grounding myself  and finding home within myself and i  think i did a pretty good job of that  and i just want to keep building on that  because you know the world is a  turbulent place and it feels like it's  only  in some ways gonna get more turbulent so  finding a place  where i can feel peace within feels like  it's gonna be pretty important and by  getting to know myself i don't mean just  like  looking deep within myself and  psychoanalyzing my history and  experiences that i've had but it's also  about like  looking forward to me like i don't  really know what like my next  step or goal or dream is i guess like  for the first time i have  the space and capacity and like empty  blank line to do that and that's  something that i want to figure out this  year and i think in previous years i was  just like too  afraid to like acknowledge that there  was a blank line  after the thing that i had already  defined and so  it used to just like fill me with  anxiety and being like oh my gosh but i  don't know where i'm headed but this  year i feel like  it's like yeah i don't know where i'm  headed and that's fine because i'm going  to enjoy the journey and i think this is  like the logical next step  after going full-time content creator  last year because i finally like  climbed the mountain that i've been  always wanting to climb and now i'm at  the top  i can see all the other mountains around  me for the first time so yeah i don't  really know which direction i want to  head towards but  i want to figure out what feels right to  me like this is me  paving my own path for the first time  without really having any answers  and taking inspiration from lots of  different people and  i just want to figure that out this year  i guess  and i think the grounding part in the  process is really important because  that's how i'm going to stay  true to myself and make sure that the  path that i want to go on is one that  feels authentically me and it's  something that i truly want to do  but who knows what 2021 has in store for  us  i think for the first time in many  months there are glimmers of hope that  we can see on the horizon which  is really kind of like feels like  there's sunshine on our faces or we see  the light at the end of the tunnel here  so i'm feeling pretty good about it i'm  excited  and let's do this thing if you have any  2021  goals aspirations intentions that you've  identified or you're working to identify  then leave them in the comments down  below i'd love to hear from you and as  always don't forget to like this video  and subscribe  i've got a lot of videos and a lot of  plans for this year which  definitely are still works in progress  but i'm really excited about the year to  come and i hope you'll join me in the  journey  i sincerely hope you all are doing well  and staying safe and i will see you next  time  bye
 

